id: pm-ffz0a9
title: "Harness provenance can only be declared as environment variables, so the model the primary harness publishes in its own session record is inexpressible: 900 of 900 explicit entries still record model null while effort resolves"
description: "Automatic identity is meant to record which model acted, so an agent never types an identity flag. Harness and reasoning effort are recorded correctly today. The model is not, and cannot be, because of how signal sources are declared rather than because of which keys are declared.\n\nHarnessSignalDescriptor (src/core/shared/author.ts:58) can express exactly four kinds of evidence: environment_keys, model_environment_keys, session_environment_keys, provenance_environment_keys, plus argv_markers and client_names for identifying the harness itself. Every provenance dimension is therefore an environment variable by construction. analyzeAgentProvenanceDescriptorCoverage (src/sdk/provenance.ts:44) confirms the shape: coverage for a dimension is computed as whether any descriptor lists environment keys for it. A dimension a harness publishes through any other channel -- a file, a socket, a process attribute, a protocol handshake field -- is not merely undetected, it is inexpressible.\n\nMeasured at HEAD, build 2026.7.28, inside a real claude-code session:\n\n  declared model sources for claude-code   ANTHROPIC_MODEL, CLAUDE_MODEL\n  either variable present in the session    no\n  variables the harness actually publishes  CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID,\n                                            CLAUDE_EFFORT, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION,\n                                            AI_AGENT (value carries harness and version)\n\nA sandbox mutation recorded right now, with no author override:\n\n  author            harness:claude-code\n  author_source     detected\n  agent_harness     claude-code\n  agent_instance    4018c32541da6a6805d5bd7d\n  agent_provenance  model: null, effort: xhigh from environment\n  agent_model       null\n\nHarness resolves. Effort resolves. Model is null, and the corpus agrees: across every history entry carrying explicit provenance, 848 record model null and 52 record model null with an effort observation. Zero observed models across 4,353 claude-code, 1,728 codex and 155 opencode entries.\n\nThe model is not missing from the machine. It is published, on disk, keyed by a variable pm already reads. CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID is declared as this harness's session key and is set. The harness writes its own session record under a per-project directory named for the working directory, in a file named for that exact session id, and every assistant record in it carries the model identifier and the harness version. In the session that produced this item, 62 records carry model claude-opus-5 and the record header carries version 2.1.220. Joining a variable pm already reads to a file the harness already writes yields the missing dimension exactly.\n\nThis is why pm-0zcwz6, which closed correctly on what it delivered, did not change the outcome. It added environment, argv, and client model sources -- three more instances of the one channel the primary harness does not use for this dimension. Adding a fourth environment key cannot work, and the descriptor type offers nothing else to add.\n\nWhat this item owns: a second class of signal source. A descriptor should be able to declare a resolver -- a named, bounded, side-effect-free probe that reads a location derived from already-detected signals -- alongside its environment keys, with the observation recording which source produced it, exactly as effort already records source environment today.\n\nConstraints that are part of the requirement, not caveats. A probe reads local files that can contain arbitrary session content, so it must extract only the declared dimension value, never retain or copy surrounding content, be bounded in bytes and time, fail closed to null rather than erroring, and be disableable by configuration. It must never become a blocking dependency of a mutation. And the recorded provenance must distinguish a value observed from a probe from a value observed from the environment, so the corpus stays auditable.\n\nTwo adjacent observations that fall out of the same reading and belong to this item because they are the same channel question. AI_AGENT carries the harness version in the environment and AGENT_PROVENANCE_DIMENSIONS has no version dimension to receive it. CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION distinguishes a delegated sub-session from a root session, which is a role signal available in the environment right now.\n\nBoundaries. pm-rbg1qo owns which dimensions are declared for which harnesses and the absent session-topic keys; that is a question about coverage within the existing channel and stays with it. pm-0zcwz6 and pm-itsjf0 are closed and correct about what they shipped. This item is only the claim that one channel is not enough, and that the missing dimension is reachable through a second one."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
