author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "A harness signal descriptor can declare a non-environment resolver for any provenance dimension, alongside its environment keys; The claude-code descriptor resolves the model by joining its already-declared session key to the harness session record, and a live mutation records a non-null model with the source naming the probe; Provenance observations distinguish a probe-sourced value from an environment-sourced value, the way effort already records its source; A probe is bounded in bytes and time, extracts only the declared dimension, never retains surrounding content, fails closed to null, and never blocks or fails a mutation; Probing is disableable by configuration and its default is documented; A harness version dimension exists and is populated for at least one harness that publishes it; A negative control proves the descriptor coverage analysis reports a dimension as uncovered when neither an environment key nor a resolver can supply it"
