comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T22:39:22.071Z","harness:claude-code","Live re-measure 2026-07-28 on this repository's own tracker, taken from the most recent entry of a real mutation stream rather than from a synthetic probe. The recorded provenance is:\n\n  author           harness:claude-code\n  author_source    detected\n  agent_harness    claude-code\n  agent_instance   present, a 24-character digest\n  agent_provenance model null, effort {value: xhigh, source: environment}\n\nSo three of the four dimensions the maintainer directive asks for are live and correct - harness, instance, and thinking level - and are obtained with no PM_AUTHOR and no --author, which is the mandate. The two that remain absent are exactly the two this item and pm-itsjf0 own: model stays null because the harness publishes no model key for any resolver to read, and session topic and role are carried by zero entries because no environment signal exists to detect them. Nothing about the measurement has changed since it was filed; recorded here so the claim rests on a current reading rather than a recalled one.\n"
  "2026-07-29T21:26:19.526Z","harness:codex","Live provenance census 2026-07-29: pm activity read all 41,391 immutable events. 7,879 entries carry detected author provenance, with harness counts claude-code 4,608, codex 2,418, and opencode 155; 307 entries currently carry an effort value. Model is null on all 41,391 entries. This confirms the issue remains current and corpus-wide; no duplicate provenance item was created."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T09:22:12.536Z","harness:claude-code","Live provenance re-measure 2026-07-30, from a create entry written by this session. The entry carries: author harness:claude-code, author_source detected, agent_harness claude-code, agent_instance a 24-hex handle, and agent_provenance with effort resolved as value xhigh source environment. It carries model null.\n\nSo the split this item names is stable and unchanged: the thinking level resolves from the environment and the model does not, because the harness publishes no model key of any kind. There is still no field anywhere on the entry for session topic or session role, so the maintainer request for an identity that reads like a model plus a thinking level plus a session role is currently one third delivered, one third blocked on a non-environment channel, and one third without a schema slot at all."
body: ""
